jobs.description:
Our client – an innovative and fast-growing company in the fintech sector – is on a mission to redefine digital operations through smart automation. As part of their growth, they’re seeking a **Business Process Automation Engineer** to join their Data Team and help drive the next generation of internal workflow automation.

This is an exciting opportunity for a problem-solver with a strong technical foundation in no-code/low-code tools and a passion for streamlining processes.

# Key Responsibilities:

* Design and implement scalable automation workflows using **n8n** and other automation platforms;

* Collaborate with business stakeholders to gather requirements and translate them into technical automation solutions;

* Integrate workflows with data platforms and APIs (e.g., BigQuery, internal tools);

* Monitor, maintain, and troubleshoot existing automations for stability and scalability;

* Identify new opportunities for automation and process optimization across departments;

* Develop custom connectors and integrations (REST APIs, webhooks, cloud services);

* Document workflows, data flows, and technical specifications.

,

# What We’re Looking For:

* Hands-on experience with **n8n**, Zapier, [Make.com](https://make.com), or similar platforms;

* Solid understanding of **APIs**, **webhooks**, and **JSON;**

* Experience with scripting or backend languages ([Node.js](https://node.js), Python, etc.) is a strong plus;

* Familiarity with databases or data warehouses (SQL, BigQuery);

* Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment;

* Strong analytical mindset and a systems-thinking approach;

* Excellent communication and documentation skills.

,

# Bonus Points For:

* Experience in **fintech** or banking operations;

* Familiarity with **Jira**, **Confluence**, or similar tools;

* Understanding of **data privacy** and **compliance frameworks** (e.g., GDPR, ISO27001, DORA).

,

# What’s in It for You:

* Paid vacation, birthday leave, and tenure-based time-off perks;

* Flexible work arrangements;

* Private health insurance (post-probation);

* Annual trust day for personal matters and dedicated learning time;

* A strong culture of recognition, with awards, gifts, and sponsored events;

* Financial support and extra leave for key life events (e.g., weddings, childbirth);

* Regular team events and social activities;

* Salary starting from €3,300/month gross, with potential adjustments based on experience.

