Scale3C is revolutionizing digital operations in fintech using smart automation in a vibrant collaborative atmosphere.

The company is building innovative solutions to transform industries with bespoke websites, web apps, and mobile applications, driven by cutting-edge technology and user-centric design.

Scale3C collaborates with clients worldwide, focusing on those in the USA, Canada, France, and Lithuania, showcasing diverse and enriching project experiences.

The Business Process Automation Engineer will design and implement scalable automation workflows using no-code/low-code tools within a fintech innovation-driven environment.

Candidates need hands-on experience with n8n, Zapier, or similar platforms, a solid understanding of APIs, webhooks, and JSON, and excellent communication and documentation skills.

Experience with Node.js or Python is a strong plus. Familiarity with SQL, BigQuery, and backend languages is desired for seamless workflow automation.

The position offers a competitive gross salary starting from €3,300/month. Remuneration can be adjusted based on the candidate's experience level.

The role is based in Vilnius with hybrid work options, allowing flexibility and work-life balance while being part of dynamic projects and teams.

Standout perks include private health insurance, flexible work arrangements, financial support for key life events, and a strong culture of recognition.

Embrace a career at Scale3C where technology and innovative processes define the future. Join a team dedicated to pushing boundaries in the fintech sector.

Who our client is:

Pulsetto is creating cutting-edge neuromodulation devices designed to enhance well-being through innovative wearable technology. We are looking for a Back-End Developer who has a strong understanding of databases, API’s, and hardware firmware integration to join our growing team.

As a Back-End Developer, you will be tasked with developing and maintaining the backend of our app, designing efficient databases to manage large sets of wearable data, and ensuring smooth communication between the software and hardware. You will play a key role in the functionality of the device’s firmware and backend infrastructure.

**Location: Vilnius (Onsite, with potential for remote work).**

# Requirements:

* Mid-to-senior level experience working with .NET framework;

* Strong understanding of PostgreSQL and database design for handling large datasets;

* Basic knowledge of Arduino and firmware interaction is sufficient;

* Familiarity with Bluetooth protocols is beneficial;

* Experience working with Google Cloud Platform (GCP) or similar cloud platforms;

* Ability to troubleshoot, debug, and optimize backend processes;

* Strong problem-solving skills with attention to efficiency and scalability;

* Ability to work onsite in Lithuania, with the possibility of remote work after workflows are established.

,

# Responsibilities:

* Develop and maintain backend services;

* Design and optimize database structures for efficient data storage and retrieval of large wearable datasets;

* Esure smooth integration between firmware and software systems, with a strong focus on data handling;

* Collaborate with front-end developers to support app functionality and user experience;

* Work with Bluetooth protocols to ensure proper communication between devices and the backend;

* Help implement best practices in security, performance, and scalability.

,

# We offer:

* Work with some of the world’s leading and most recognized brands;

* Remote work;

* Agile-driven work culture;

* Strong focus on learning and development.

